<main id="main" class="reading">
  <div class="reading__inner">
    {#- DRAFT for JD's review: Mission, Vision, Values and Principles. The mission is JD's own wording. -#}
    <section class="section" id="mission">
      <p class="label">Mission</p>
      <h2>Why we <em>do this</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <p class="lede">Our goal is to help people across the country build skills that allow them to relate and connect with others more effectively.</p>
      <p class="label">Vision</p>
      <p class="soft">A healthier, more connected world: people who can stay close through the hard moments, in love, with friends, at work and in community, and an earth that gets to be a better, healthier playground for all of us.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="values">
      <p class="label">Values</p>
      <h2>What we <em>stand on</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <ul class="cards">
        <li class="card"><h3>Connection</h3><p>People heal and grow in relationship. We gather in person, in real rooms, because that’s where connection is practiced.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><h3>Compassion in action</h3><p>Care that does something. We hold a space free of judgment and shame, and still tell the truth.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><h3>Curiosity</h3><p>Feelings carry information and instructions. We get curious about what they’re telling us instead of judging them.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><h3>Practice</h3><p>We practice before we teach, and we teach so you can practice. Insight is a start; repetition is what changes the loop.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><h3>Choice</h3><p>You can choose differently. The defaults you were handed are a starting point, not a sentence.</p></li>
        <li class="card"><h3>Rigor in the open</h3><p>We test what works, keep what holds up, and show our sources so you can check them yourself.</p></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="principles">
      <p class="label">Principles</p>
      <h2>How we <em>hold the room</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span class="steps__num">01</span><h3>You’re the scientist</h3><p>You run the experiment on your own life. We bring the instruments and the room.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">02</span><h3>We don’t fix people</h3><p>Nothing about you needs fixing. We help you see the patterns you live inside and practice something new.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">03</span><h3>Every exercise has an opt-out</h3><p>You choose what you share and what you try. What’s shared in the room stays in the room.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">04</span><h3>Clear agreements</h3><p>We say how the room works before we start, and keep a plan for when things get real.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">05</span><h3>Speak from the heart</h3><p>Honest feedback, given with care. The right people stay.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="label">What we do</p>
      <h2>Five ways we <em>work with you</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <p class="soft">Most of us talk about our patterns with a therapist, a coach or a friend. Fewer of us get to actually test something new, with honest feedback, and keep iterating until it holds. Everything we offer is built around that practice, because insight is a start and practice is what changes the loop.</p>
      <ul class="cards">
        <li class="card">
          <p class="label">Coach</p>
          <h3>One-on-one and couples</h3>
          <p>Level-Up Sessions that name the loop you keep running, shift it where talking alone can’t reach, and give you something to practice the same day. Follow-ups and support between sessions, so the change has somewhere to land.</p>
          <div class="card__actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/level-up/">Level-Up Sessions</a></div>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <p class="label">Facilitator</p>
          <h3>Practice Labs and workshops</h3>
          <p>Hands-on group labs where you come as the scientist of your own life: you practice, notice what happens, and take the skill home. Every exercise has an opt-out, and what’s shared in the room stays in the room.</p>
          <div class="card__actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/love/">The Love Lab</a></div>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <p class="label">Event planner</p>
          <h3>Dinners, retreats and ceremonies</h3>
          <p>Candlelit lab dinners, multi-day retreats, lunch-and-learns, and ceremonies for the turning points of a life. We plan the room, the food, the flow and the care, so the people in it can do the real work.</p>
          <div class="card__actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Plan something with us</a></div>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <p class="label">Consultant</p>
          <h3>Teams and leaders</h3>
          <p>The same loops that run a relationship run a team. We bring two decades of engineering leadership to the human side of how groups decide, disagree and deliver: working sessions, offsites and leadership coaching.</p>
          <div class="card__actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/contact/">Talk about your team</a></div>
        </li>
        <li class="card">
          <p class="label">Leader</p>
          <h3>Building rooms people trust</h3>
          <p>JD has led engineering organizations, volunteer care teams and community gatherings. That experience shows up in how we hold a room: clear agreements, steady presence, and a plan for when things get real.</p>
          <div class="card__actions"><a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/about/jd/">About JD</a></div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="label">How it works</p>
      <h2>See · Shift · <em>Prove</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <p class="soft">Whether it’s a two-hour session or a five-day retreat, the method underneath is the same.</p>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><span class="steps__num">01</span><h3>See</h3><p>Name the loop that keeps running, in one clear sentence. Not a diagnosis. A starting point.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">02</span><h3>Shift</h3><p>Change how that loop runs, where talking alone can’t reach.</p></li>
        <li><span class="steps__num">03</span><h3>Prove</h3><p>Practice with real people until the change holds.</p></li>
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <p class="label">Where it comes from</p>
      <h2>Rigor, <em>and roots</em></h2>
      <hr class="rule">
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Practice Labs is JD Carlston’s method. It draws on her study with Dr. Robert Dee McDonald, NLP architect, clinical researcher and co-founder of the <a href="https://teloscenter.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Telos Healing Center</a>, and weaves his teaching together with attachment science, nervous-system work, humanistic therapy and an engineer’s habit of testing what actually works.</p>
        <p>We keep our sources in the open. <a href="/lineage/">Research Roots</a> walks through the research and the people behind each idea we use, with every study linked.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</main>

